This project ships or downloads data from the following sources. See docs/licensing.md for
the terms each carries and how the project meets them.

U.S. Census Bureau — gazetteer files, 2020 relationship files, and the Data API.
  Works of the United States Government (17 U.S.C. § 105); no copyright. Products that use the
  Census Bureau Data API must state: "This product uses the Census Bureau Data API but is not
  endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau."

U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics — LABSTAT area code tables, the Public Data API, and the QCEW
  open data feed. Works of the United States Government; no copyright. BLS asks that the retrieval
  date be cited and states that "BLS.gov cannot vouch for the data or analyses derived from these
  data after the data have been retrieved from BLS.gov."

U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, HUD User — the HUD User Data API (Fair Market
  Rents, Income Limits, MTSP limits, CHAS, Picture of Subsidized Households). Works of the United
  States Government; no copyright. This product uses the HUD User Data API but is not endorsed or
  certified by HUD User.

U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis — the BEA Data API (Regional personal income, GDP, regional price
  parities). Works of the United States Government; no copyright. This product uses the Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA) Data API but is not endorsed or certified by BEA.

Missouri Census Data Center (MCDC), University of Missouri — Geocorr 2022 place-to-county
  correlation output, vendored as packages/geography-build/src/data/geocorr/*. Geocorr is produced
  by MCDC (a Census Bureau State Data Center partner, sponsored by the Missouri State Library,
  published by the University of Missouri Center for Health Policy) from public-domain Census
  Bureau block data. MCDC publishes no licence or terms for Geocorr output; the project credits
  MCDC as the source of the allocation factors. Suggested citation: Missouri Census Data Center,
  Geocorr 2022: Geographic Correspondence Engine, https://mcdc.missouri.edu/applications/geocorr2022.html
  (retrieved 2026-09-17).

Design inspiration (no code copied): cyanheads/bls-labor-mcp-server (Apache-2.0),
